---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Run the requests under files or folders and report the results

Usage: rustman run [OPTIONS] [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...
          Request files or folders to run (default: the current directory)

Options:
      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Total timeout per request, replacing settings.timeout_ms: 500ms, 5s, 2m, or a number of milliseconds

  -k, --insecure
          Do not verify TLS certificates (exchanges are flagged insecure)

      --no-history
          Do not record the exchanges in history

  -u, --update-snapshots
          Overwrite snapshots that differ from the response (not in CI mode)

      --ci
          CI mode: never write snapshots, and fail on a missing one (also on when the CI variable is true or 1)

      --bail[=<SCOPE>]
          Skip the remaining requests after the first failed or errored one; --bail=iteration skips only the rest of the failing iteration
          
          [possible values: run, iteration]

      --filter <FILTER>
          Run only matching requests: tag:<name>, or a glob over request ids such as 'users/*' (repeatable; a request matching any runs)

      --iterations <N>
          Run the selected requests this many times (default 1)

      --data <FILE>
          Run the selected requests once per row of a CSV or JSON file, with the row's values as variables (default: the folder's _collection.yaml data)

      --no-data
          Ignore the data file a _collection.yaml names

      --data-label <COLUMN>
          Label each iteration with this column's value in reports (default: row <n>)

      --secret-columns <A,B>
          Data columns whose values are secrets and are redacted in every output, besides those named like password, token, secret or api_key

      --parallel <N>
          Run up to N folders at once; requests in one folder stay in order unless its _collection.yaml sets parallel: true
          
          [default: 1]

      --reporter <FORMAT[:PATH]>
          Report format, optionally written to a file: pretty, json, junit or tap, as in json or junit:out/junit.xml (repeatable; default: pretty on stdout)

      --report <FORMAT[=PATH]>
          Also render the report as json, junit, markdown, html or sarif, written to a file or stdout, as in html=out/report.html (repeatable)

      --max-events <N>
          GraphQL and JSON-RPC subscriptions stop after N events (default: each request's max_events, else 10)

      --duration <DURATION>
          GraphQL and JSON-RPC subscriptions stop after this long (default: each request's duration or max_duration_ms, else 30s)

      --trust
          Spawn the workspace's stdio MCP servers that are not trusted yet, and record the approvals

      --viz
          Show the run live in the graphical viz companion (rustman-viz); the run continues without it when it is not installed

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
